upstream_title: Goldbach30 / Goldbach29 FRACTRAN reduction pair and halting-semantics provenance

attribution_boundary:
  Mike Dupont / meta-introspector owns the upstream Goldbach30 and Goldbach29
  constructions, their 30-to-29 fraction reduction, abstract machines,
  FRACTRAN programs, and Lean proofs fstep_enc. The later source-visible
  Goldbach29 theorem goldbachProg_halts_iff remains Mike/meta-introspector's
  formal authority. The Goldbach30 commit narrative also claims a matching
  theorem, but DASHI does not promote that narrative to formal theorem authority
  because its claimed Main.lean/Loops.lean files are absent from the audited
  exact commit tree and the known paths have no GitHub commit history.
  DASHI owns only this provenance/audit receipt plus its independent
  observer/fibre translation, source-faithful arithmetic reconstruction of the
  success macro, checkpoint quotient, and DASHI-native consumer/cost theorems.

literal_rule_delta_at_construction_commit:
  - rules 1 through 25 are identical annotated rules in both Program.lean blobs
  - Goldbach30 rule 26 is NT.B[f] -> SA
  - Goldbach30 rule 27 is NT.B[b,c] -> RA.A[a,d^2,f]
  - Goldbach30 rules 28..30 are SA[a] -> SB[b,c], SB -> SA, SA[c] -> RA.A[a^2,d^2,f]
  - Goldbach29 rule 26 is NT.B[f,a] -> SB[b,c]
  - Goldbach29 rule 27 is NT.B[f] -> NT2.B[a,b]
  - Goldbach29 rule 28 is the same failure rule NT.B[b,c] -> RA.A[a,d^2,f]
  - Goldbach29 rule 29 is SB -> NT.B[f]
  - therefore all post-prefix differences are confined to the success routing;
    the failure transition is retained literally with only its list position shifted

source_reachable_success_guard:
  - NT.B success is reached only after earlier s/g restoration branches are exhausted
  - exact DASHI macro contract therefore fixes s=0, g=0 and verdict f=1
  - tested a is structurally positive
  - c may be zero on entry; canonical first success has a=2,b=2,c=0,f=1
  - arbitrary f>1 is intentionally excluded because Goldbach29 would re-enter
    the success branch after staging rather than satisfy the one-pass quotient

external_facts_used:
  - Goldbach30 has 30 fractions and 11 control states
  - Goldbach29 has 29 fractions and 10 control states
  - the first 25 annotated rules are shared before the success/failure tail
  - the SA control state is removed in Goldbach29
  - Goldbach30 success uses NT.B -> SA, the SA/SB transfer loop, then SA -> RA.A
  - Goldbach29 success reroutes the transfer through NT.B/SB, stages through
    NT2.B, and reuses the existing NT.B b c -> RA.A transition
  - each committed Program.lean proves one encoded FRACTRAN step matches one
    abstract astep step (fstep_enc)
  - at goldbach29_semantic_source_revision, Goldbach29/Main.lean contains
    theorem goldbachProg_halts_iff: the 29-fraction program halts from N0 iff
    there is an even n >= 4 with no representation as a sum of two primes
  - Goldbach30 commit 7added5000a75226a834ba7aab08a7380f0c70b3 narratively
    claims the corresponding Goldbach30 theorem and no-sorry build
  - recursive tree audit of that exact commit finds no Goldbach30/Main.lean or
    Goldbach30/Loops.lean; GitHub path-history queries for the known paths are
    also empty, so that claim remains development-narrative evidence

path_provenance_note:
  The construction commit itself records Goldbach29 under the d3e01240 UUID
  directory. A later/user-supplied link used another UUID path; DASHI does not
  rewrite commit-native provenance to that later path.

non_claims:
  - this receipt does not vendor-copy AGPL source into DASHI
  - this receipt does not claim DASHI authorship of Goldbach30 or Goldbach29
  - imported Lean theorem authority is not an Agda proof
  - a commit-message theorem claim without its source artifact is not imported
    formal theorem authority
  - the DASHI checkpoint theorem is not yet a cross-prover same-object proof
    about the pinned Lean/FRACTRAN carriers
  - goldbachProg_halts_iff is an equivalence to a counterexample; it is not a
    proof that no counterexample exists and therefore does not prove Goldbach
  - this receipt alone does not prove Goldbach30/29 whole-machine weak bisimulation
